--- Sentence//end
id: 509
r#  92272  1733  37
p: .
t. 
|  When interpreting a sentence, we need to queue up words
|  in a well-determined order, each acting as a
|  kind of conceptual transform applied to
.  syntheses borne from precedent words


--- Sentence/switch
id: 510
r#  92273  1733  38


--- Sentence//end
id: 510
r#  92475  1737  43
p: .
t. 
|   To sequence
|  which word comes on the stage, when, demands a
|  rigorous set of phrase-bounding and morphosyntactic
|  conventions, which gestate within language
.  under the guise of syntactic proscriptions


--- Sentence/switch
